1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,008
[audio slowed down]

2
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:10,802
[water droplets patter]

3
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,480
[Wen] <i>Yi-hsuan,
do you remember
the name Ching?</i>

4
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:24,316
[dramatic music playing]

5
00:00:27,152 --> 00:00:29,321
Your real mom is Chao Yu-jung.

6
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:32,824
<i>She had an affair
with Chang Da-chin.</i>

7
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:37,579
Chang Da-chin is your father.

8
00:00:43,794 --> 00:00:46,504
Come on, Cheng-chun.
Give me Garlic Shrimps
for Table 3.

9
00:00:46,505 --> 00:00:47,673
I need one more minute!

10
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:51,218
Hurry up! We're busy as hell!

11
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:52,844
Is Three-cup Chicken ready
for Table 8?

12
00:00:53,095 --> 00:00:55,013
[Feng] Not yet.
The sauce hasn't reduced.

13
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,764
Give me Chinese
Yam Pork Rib Soup then.

14
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:58,809
What, again?
We have no Chinese yam.
Don't take any more orders!

15
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:02,354
Give me anything you have, okay?
Customers are complaining.

16
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:07,276
[Wen] <i>Yu-jung was capable.</i>

17
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:10,529
<i>She became
Chang Da-chin's secretary.</i>

18
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:13,740
<i>They had an affair
and gave birth to you.</i>

19
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:21,582
I don't have a dad.
And I don't know
what a father's love is.

20
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:24,750
[Chang Ta-chin] <i>I know you.
Good job in marketing.</i>

21
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:26,044
I think you're talented.

22
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:27,838
Do you want to work
for Chang Xin?

23
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:31,216
[Chin-nan]
Give me the fried rice.

24
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,259
- Thank you!
- [Yu-li] Okay! Go!

25
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:35,803
Here, Boss!
Give me Fried Rice
with Sausage and Squid!

26
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,430
[whirring]

27
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:39,390
Another order
of Chinese Yam Pork Rib Soup.

28
00:01:39,391 --> 00:01:43,769
Yi-hsuan is fetching some,
isn't she?
Call her and see how it's going.

29
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,897
[thunder rumbles]

30
00:01:46,732 --> 00:01:48,442
[Chang Ta-chin]
<i>Think about it.</i>

31
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:51,570
Is Chou Lu-yung
really nice to you?

32
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:53,905
[Lu-yung]
<i>I'll be right here with you.</i>

33
00:01:54,156 --> 00:01:57,283
[music continues]

34
00:01:57,284 --> 00:02:00,120
[thunder rumbling]

35
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:11,632
[muffled chatter]

36
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:18,805
- [Chin-nan] I'll take
the Garlic Shrimps.
- [Yu-li] Go.

37
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:21,516
Hey. What happened to you?

38
00:02:22,476 --> 00:02:23,644
[Yi-hsuan] Chou Lu-yung?

39
00:02:30,609 --> 00:02:31,943
Let's go, Feng.

40
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:39,660
Are you alright?

41
00:02:39,785 --> 00:02:42,913
[soft dramatic music playing]

42
00:02:53,924 --> 00:02:56,927
[indistinct chatter]

43
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:03,975
[Yi-hsuan] I love you.

44
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:09,522
But what if my dad
is your worst enemy?

45
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:11,899
Can you still love me?

46
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,527
What does that mean?

47
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:16,822
Wen told me...

48
00:03:19,658 --> 00:03:22,327
my mom was
Chang Da-chin's mistress,

49
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:25,580
and I'm his
illegitimate daughter.

50
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:29,209
Are you still willing
to love me?

51
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:31,002
[music continues]

52
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:57,237
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

53
00:03:57,362 --> 00:04:01,825
[singing in Mandarin]

54
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,035
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

55
00:04:04,286 --> 00:04:06,370
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

56
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:08,415
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

57
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,542
[singing in Mandarin]

58
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:14,588
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

59
00:04:14,713 --> 00:04:17,549
[singing in Mandarin]

60
00:04:23,555 --> 00:04:27,517
CHANG CHIEN-YUAN

61
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:55,670
[gentle music playing]

62
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,806
[Chin-lai] Okay,
I know you love spicy food.

63
00:05:05,931 --> 00:05:09,768
- Yeah, and the minced celery...
- [door opens]

64
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:15,356
Mom, you're home.

65
00:05:15,357 --> 00:05:16,441
Yeah.

66
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:19,444
- Off work?
- Hi, Uncle Chin-lai.

67
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,696
Why are you eating
expired rice balls again?

68
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,950
They're just about to expire.
Besides, it's bread.

69
00:05:26,618 --> 00:05:29,829
Fine. I'll eat the bread
and give you fried rice noodles
in exchange.

70
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:31,581
That's it. No haggling.

71
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:37,753
Uncle, did you press
the rice noodles with a spatula?

72
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:38,922
They're crispy.

73
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:42,550
You're turning
into a food critic.

74
00:05:42,551 --> 00:05:45,553
Of course.
With a great chef like you
cooking for me for years,

75
00:05:45,554 --> 00:05:47,513
I know how to eat, at least.

76
00:05:47,514 --> 00:05:50,684
Yeah. Since you were little,
I've been feeding you
with my food,

77
00:05:50,809 --> 00:05:52,102
and now, you're all grown up.

78
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:54,646
- I'm all grown up.
- You're all grown up.

79
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:57,481
[laughter]

80
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:58,983
[knock on door]

81
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:01,069
[secretary] Ma'am,
the meeting will start soon.

82
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,654
Okay. I'll be there.

83
00:06:03,655 --> 00:06:06,658
[tense music playing]

84
00:06:08,952 --> 00:06:12,122
[Yi-hsuan] What Chang Xin
needs now is to target
online and younger audiences.

85
00:06:13,123 --> 00:06:16,543
We'll not only grow big,
but also become
a star enterprise.

86
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:19,337
- We want to be eye-catching.
- Where's the chairman?

87
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:23,383
- [Yi-hsuan] Being eye-catching
converts into market share.
- He won't show up today.

88
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:25,844
I think the chairman
has approved the proposal

89
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:28,013
and authorized Yi-hsuan
to present and execute it.

90
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:33,851
So, we'll go into remote areas
to connect
with the underprivileged.

91
00:06:33,852 --> 00:06:38,565
We'll take on
social responsibility
to rebuild our corporate image.

92
00:06:43,695 --> 00:06:45,697
I'm curious.

93
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:51,870
You came here because you found
what you wanted in Chang Xin?

94
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:57,042
Chou Lu-yung dumped me.

95
00:06:57,167 --> 00:07:00,462
I want him to know
how he'll do without me.

96
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,716
That's all?

97
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:06,800
That's my initial motive.

98
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:09,888
My mid-term goal is to replace
Wu Hsiu-wen in the company.

99
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:12,473
[music continues]

100
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:14,476
[laughs]

101
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:19,856
I believe you can do it.

102
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:29,532
[indistinct chatter]

103
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:47,759
What are you here for?

104
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:50,679
To save Chang Xin.

105
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:56,434
The chairman hired me
because he thinks I'm talented.

106
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:59,771
What about Jin Lai Hao?
Aren't you with them?

107
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:07,487
I don't love Chou Lu-yung
anymore.

108
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:10,490
I think my future is here.

109
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:13,702
How could you abandon them?

110
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:16,913
What are you so afraid of?

111
00:08:17,831 --> 00:08:20,125
Am I making you
uncomfortable here?

112
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:26,965
You don't know
what you're doing at all.

113
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:28,550
Of course, I know.

114
00:08:31,553 --> 00:08:34,639
Be careful.
I'm ready to replace you.

115
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,028
[sighs]

116
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:55,159
The ecology of our planet
is facing severe threats.

117
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:57,829
We'll launch
the Chang Xin Green Commitment.

118
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:02,875
From research and development,
sourcing, to production
and marketing,

119
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:06,086
we'll uphold a deep respect
for nature.

120
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:10,007
The Chang Xin Green Commitment
starts now. Thank you.

121
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:13,053
[applause]

122
00:09:19,017 --> 00:09:23,688
And now, we will be presenting
the Chang Xin
Green Scholarships.

123
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:27,567
Let's take a group photo.
Show a big smile.

124
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:30,027
[classical music playing]

125
00:09:30,028 --> 00:09:33,239
Chang Da-chin,
you dishonest businessman!

126
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:37,911
Can you explain to us
how Chang Xin colludes
with middlemen

127
00:09:38,036 --> 00:09:39,912
to exploit us farmers?

128
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:41,789
- Chang Xin, you're hypocrites!
- Can you explain that to us?

129
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:44,042
- Step down, Chang Da-chin!
Step down!
- Calm down, please.

130
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:46,711
- You liar!
- Step down!

131
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:49,881
Calm down. Calm down, please.

132
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:52,300
Get out.

133
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,762
Get out.

134
00:09:57,222 --> 00:09:58,807
Security?

135
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:02,393
Get out, please.

136
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,772
[protester] You'll go to hell!
Go to hell!

137
00:10:06,773 --> 00:10:08,233
You exploit farmers!

138
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,276
You'll pay for it!

139
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:13,153
- Are you alright?
- Yeah.

140
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:17,366
[protester] You exploit farmers!
You're hypocrites!
You exploit farmers!

141
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:21,412
Many things we do
are misunderstood
by some people.

142
00:10:21,663 --> 00:10:23,915
You need to get used to it.

143
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:26,292
If you're in trouble,

144
00:10:28,086 --> 00:10:29,754
ask Hsiu-wen for help.

145
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:34,925
If you have questions
or are not used to something,

146
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:37,262
just tell me. It's alright.

147
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:40,765
I'll get used to it
because I'm looking
at the big picture.

148
00:10:44,853 --> 00:10:46,354
[Chang Ta-chin]
It's fine. Go get busy.

149
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:51,860
Hsiu-wen, you stay.

150
00:10:54,696 --> 00:10:57,740
[tense music playing]

151
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:02,871
[sighs]

152
00:11:03,872 --> 00:11:05,290
What do you think about her?

153
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:09,042
I don't trust her.

154
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:10,670
[grunts]

155
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,800
Because she's young

156
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,886
or she used to work
for Chou Lu-yung?

157
00:11:22,182 --> 00:11:23,308
Both.

158
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:28,353
If it's simply
a matter of trust, don't worry.

159
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:30,273
I have my own plans. Hmm?

160
00:11:33,193 --> 00:11:34,319
Yes, sir.

161
00:11:35,278 --> 00:11:37,989
[sharp inhales, winces]

162
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:42,160
[coughs, sighs]

163
00:11:54,172 --> 00:11:57,175
[gentle music playing]

164
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:03,932
But what if my dad
is your worst enemy?

165
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:07,977
<i>Can you still love me?</i>

166
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:19,280
<i>I don't know why
the fried rice you made
really touched me.</i>

167
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:24,869
<i>Because I feel
that you're worth
betting my life on.</i>

168
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,746
<i>That's my instinct.</i>

169
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:32,377
You will need me.
I'll be your restaurant manager.

170
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:34,962
<i>Whoever tries to mess
with my co-workers,</i>

171
00:12:34,963 --> 00:12:37,215
I'll smash it
right back twice as hard.

172
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:39,300
That's me, Chao Yi-hsuan.

173
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,387
<i>You should say</i>

174
00:12:42,512 --> 00:12:45,556
I'm your star
in the darkness of the night.

175
00:12:45,807 --> 00:12:48,810
[dramatic music playing]

176
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:55,149
[sizzling]

177
00:12:59,404 --> 00:13:00,989
[pained grunts]

178
00:13:06,119 --> 00:13:07,245
What's wrong?

179
00:13:09,831 --> 00:13:10,915
Are you alright?

180
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:13,251
Are you burned?

181
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:18,089
Be careful, Boss.
You make a living
with your hands.

182
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:25,096
[Chin-nan] Boss,
be a man and get her back.

183
00:13:36,274 --> 00:13:38,109
[sighs]

184
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:44,907
Look at you...

185
00:13:46,451 --> 00:13:48,453
It's okay. You'll be fine.

186
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:51,956
[Yu-li] Pull yourself together.

187
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:02,633
What the hell, Chou Lu-yung?

188
00:14:02,884 --> 00:14:05,177
Haven't you posted anything new?

189
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:06,596
YOU'VE GOT A NEW MESSAGE.

190
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:09,514
YU-LI: WHY DID YOU LEAVE?
CHAO YI-HSUAN. WHERE ARE YOU?

191
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:12,477
WHY LEAVE ME ON READ?
CHAO YI-HSUAN, REPLY TO ME NOW.

192
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:14,604
[birds chirping]

193
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:17,899
[singer singing
in foreign language]

194
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:20,985
[sighs]

195
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:35,625
Chang Xin has always been about
putting people first.

196
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,459
In this recent
cooking competition,

197
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,337
Chang Xin achieved great success
and built a reputation online.

198
00:14:40,338 --> 00:14:42,255
- [pained grunts]
- We'd like to know, sir,

199
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:45,509
how has the competition
influenced the company overall?

200
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:50,390
CHANG DA-CHIN,
CHAIRMAN OF CHANG XIN GROUP

201
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:54,059
[grunts]

202
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:57,522
Although Chang Xin
has a long history,

203
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:00,524
we're...

204
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:02,235
[dramatic music playing]

205
00:15:03,403 --> 00:15:05,905
keeping up with the times.

206
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:09,033
In short,

207
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:12,537
mutual prosperity and benefit
is Chang Xin's...

208
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,671
social responsibility
and corporate mission.

209
00:15:22,964 --> 00:15:25,549
[host] Times are changing.
Generations are shifting.

210
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:28,886
We know Chang Xin encountered
some crises not long ago...

211
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:33,432
[audio distorted]
And you made some
decisive decisions, sir.

212
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:37,228
In order to revive Chang Xin,
you've worked very hard, sir.

213
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:40,440
What I'd like to know is, sir,
could you tell us

214
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:44,444
what are the new prospects
for Chang Xin in the future?

215
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:49,365
[suspenseful music playing]

216
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:01,377
[quietly]
About Chang Xin's future...

217
00:16:02,628 --> 00:16:04,255
[sighs]

218
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,049
[indistinct chatter]

219
00:16:14,724 --> 00:16:16,516
We'll talk about it later.

220
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:17,977
Are you alright, sir?

221
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:20,563
[groaning]

222
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:26,611
- [Secretary Chin] Sir?
- [camera shutters clicking]

223
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:28,236
[Secretary Chin] Sir?

224
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:30,281
Sir?

225
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:33,367
Stop taking photos.
Call an ambulance!

226
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:37,955
[reporter] <i>Chang Xin Chairman
Chang Da-chin
suddenly collapsed.</i>

227
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:41,374
<i>...sparking stock price
volatility and a power
shake-up at Chang Xin...</i>

228
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:44,377
<i>Is this tied
to internal power struggles?</i>

229
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:46,506
<i>How will they recover
investor confidence?</i>

230
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:52,385
We were backed into a corner.

231
00:16:52,386 --> 00:16:55,598
Never thought that
Chairman Chang would collapse.

232
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,602
Did you find out
what's wrong with him?

233
00:17:00,811 --> 00:17:03,188
[Shu-min] They're tight-lipped,

234
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:05,066
only saying he's recuperating.

235
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:10,154
But at least for now,
the situation
is advantageous to us.

236
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:14,617
Do you have enough shares?

237
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:19,330
I fell into Chairman Chang's
trap and lost quite a lot,

238
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:22,208
but some shareholders
are swaying now.

239
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:27,004
So, we're holding
a shareholders' meeting?

240
00:17:27,129 --> 00:17:28,672
Mm-hmm.

241
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:31,424
The press is taking wild guesses
about his condition.

242
00:17:31,425 --> 00:17:33,385
Things are unstable now.

243
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:37,515
If I can convince
some key shareholders,
our chances are good.

244
00:17:39,684 --> 00:17:41,727
Who else might join us?

245
00:17:44,105 --> 00:17:46,189
It's not time yet.

246
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,818
I'll tell you when we're ready.

247
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:52,238
[birds chirping]

248
00:17:59,537 --> 00:18:01,163
- Doc?
- Hmm?

249
00:18:01,664 --> 00:18:04,207
When can I go to work?

250
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:06,210
Given your current condition,

251
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:09,171
as a doctor,
I don't want you to go out.

252
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:16,220
But I think I'm fine.

253
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,182
I don't think so.
Have a good rest.

254
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:24,645
How can I do that?

255
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,398
If I don't show up
in the office,

256
00:18:28,399 --> 00:18:29,816
the shareholders will think

257
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:32,278
it's their best chance
to replace me, you know.

258
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:38,743
Listen.

259
00:18:38,868 --> 00:18:42,495
As long as I can stand up
and walk, I'm fine.

260
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:45,124
Just prescribe me some medicine
to keep me going.

261
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,542
- Understand?
- [chuckles]

262
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:51,589
That's not the point here.
Sir, you're very weak now.

263
00:18:52,590 --> 00:18:55,635
You're killing him
if you stop him from working.

264
00:18:58,638 --> 00:19:00,639
[doctor] He can't be
too exhausted.

265
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,767
Doc, I'll take care of him
for you.

266
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:06,645
Fine. He's in your hands now.

267
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:07,855
[Yi-hsuan] Thank you, doc.

268
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:20,659
I just promised the doctor
to take care of you,

269
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,870
but now
I've bought you cigarettes.

270
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,707
My two sons together

271
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:30,460
aren't as considerate
as you are.

272
00:19:30,461 --> 00:19:33,631
Right. It's said that
daughters are better than sons.

273
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,761
Do you regret
not having a daughter?

274
00:19:41,222 --> 00:19:42,807
[chuckles]

275
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:45,893
[sighs]

276
00:19:47,645 --> 00:19:48,938
I have a daughter, in fact.

277
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:54,777
Some things happened.

278
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:58,739
She was taken away by her mom.

279
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:02,827
[dramatic music playing]

280
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:16,381
What did you do
that made them leave you?

281
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,800
She betrayed me.

282
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:31,564
Do you miss her?

283
00:20:31,689 --> 00:20:33,232
[laughs]

284
00:20:35,693 --> 00:20:37,820
I'm not a good father,
after all.

285
00:20:39,697 --> 00:20:41,406
I'm a businessman.

286
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:43,701
All I care about is
running a good business.

287
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:59,966
To be honest,
since I was little,

288
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:03,429
I've never thought
or expected to be the successor.

289
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:09,727
But now,
with my brother in jail,

290
00:21:09,852 --> 00:21:11,479
and my dad sick,

291
00:21:12,772 --> 00:21:16,025
you want me to betray my dad?

292
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:20,321
It doesn't seem
logical to me at all.

293
00:21:23,449 --> 00:21:26,035
You don't look like
a naive kid to me.

294
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:30,289
You'll study abroad.

295
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:34,585
Do you think when you're back,
you'll still have the influence?

296
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:38,838
If we don't change the game

297
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,424
and completely restructure
the company now,

298
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:45,596
will the future of Chang Xin
meet your expectations?

299
00:21:57,942 --> 00:21:59,944
[IV stand rolling]

300
00:22:02,404 --> 00:22:03,489
Hi, Dad.

301
00:22:04,532 --> 00:22:05,866
Have a seat.

302
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:08,869
[sighs]

303
00:22:09,954 --> 00:22:11,121
Thank you.

304
00:22:13,541 --> 00:22:15,626
How are you?
What did the doctor say?

305
00:22:17,086 --> 00:22:19,463
No big deal. I'll survive.

306
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:25,511
Dad, get some rest.
Health is the most
important thing.

307
00:22:25,636 --> 00:22:27,054
[chuckles]

308
00:22:28,681 --> 00:22:29,932
[sighs]

309
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:34,353
Chien-wu, tell me.

310
00:22:37,648 --> 00:22:40,693
Do you blame me for
what happened to your brother?

311
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:47,491
If you were me,
would you do that?

312
00:22:49,577 --> 00:22:52,121
For the sake of the company,
I'm with you.

313
00:22:54,456 --> 00:22:56,708
Chien-yuan made
all those troubles.

314
00:22:56,709 --> 00:22:58,961
You've cleaned up after him
for long enough.

315
00:22:59,837 --> 00:23:01,422
[laughs]

316
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:05,133
Good.

317
00:23:05,134 --> 00:23:09,554
When you make a decision
at work, don't be sentimental.

318
00:23:09,555 --> 00:23:10,681
Understand?

319
00:23:14,602 --> 00:23:17,396
If one day,
you need to cut ties with me,

320
00:23:17,521 --> 00:23:18,647
would you dare?

321
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:20,900
[dramatic music playing]

322
00:23:22,860 --> 00:23:23,903
[scoffs]

323
00:23:25,738 --> 00:23:27,031
What?

324
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:30,534
[sighs]

325
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:33,037
You don't know how to reply

326
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:36,664
because I'm your dad and you
don't want to hurt me, right?

327
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:37,958
Huh?

328
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:46,175
If you need to cut ties
with me, do it completely,
clean and sharp.

329
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:49,887
Just like how we do business,
be fast and merciless, huh?

330
00:23:50,888 --> 00:23:52,890
[Chang Ta-chin sighs]

331
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,519
[chuckles]

332
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,149
[winces]

333
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:05,903
- [pained grunts, sighs]
- Take it easy, Dad.

334
00:24:13,202 --> 00:24:16,163
Remember every word
that I'm telling you.

335
00:24:16,747 --> 00:24:18,248
[music continues]

336
00:24:19,667 --> 00:24:21,751
Even if I die tomorrow,

337
00:24:21,752 --> 00:24:24,921
your plan to go to New York
can't be delayed.

338
00:24:24,922 --> 00:24:26,590
Do you know why?

339
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:30,928
The world is huge.

340
00:24:32,096 --> 00:24:35,848
Chang Xin can't be confined
to this small island.

341
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:39,103
We need to go international.
Understand?

342
00:24:42,106 --> 00:24:45,025
[sighs, grunts]

343
00:25:00,624 --> 00:25:02,626
[keyboard tapping]

344
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:11,677
[knocks on door]

345
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:14,805
Hmm?

346
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:17,558
Got used to it, Miss Director?

347
00:25:20,019 --> 00:25:21,853
[Hsiu-wen] I think so.

348
00:25:21,854 --> 00:25:26,816
It's just that I need
to rearrange some SOPs,
the messy ones.

349
00:25:26,817 --> 00:25:28,986
- Thanks.
- The mess
my brother left behind?

350
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:31,738
I didn't say that.

351
00:25:31,739 --> 00:25:33,115
[both chuckle]

352
00:25:38,996 --> 00:25:40,706
Aren't you going
abroad next week?

353
00:25:43,167 --> 00:25:44,251
Yep.

354
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:49,048
How I envy you.
I'm longing for a trip.

355
00:25:50,674 --> 00:25:52,134
But I'm not there on a trip.

356
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:53,594
I'm sorry.

357
00:25:54,219 --> 00:25:55,846
How's it going with packing up?

358
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:02,269
I want your advice.

359
00:26:03,187 --> 00:26:04,687
On packing up?

360
00:26:04,688 --> 00:26:06,940
[both chuckle]

361
00:26:12,196 --> 00:26:14,156
I know it may sound weird,

362
00:26:16,158 --> 00:26:17,659
but I'd like to stay.

363
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:25,250
Are you worried about your dad?

364
00:26:31,215 --> 00:26:33,300
I know my dad and brother

365
00:26:34,093 --> 00:26:38,097
did something terrible
to someone who you saw
as a father.

366
00:26:41,391 --> 00:26:43,227
But we're blood relations.

367
00:26:45,354 --> 00:26:47,564
- I think I...
- You're different from them.

368
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:50,901
[dramatic music playing]

369
00:26:51,902 --> 00:26:53,736
Believe me.

370
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:55,072
You're different from them.

371
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:58,992
You're different from your dad
or your brother.

372
00:27:00,702 --> 00:27:03,831
You're a very kind-hearted,
considerate person.

373
00:27:14,967 --> 00:27:17,802
[car horn honks]

374
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:21,765
Chang Xin is so lucky
to have the two of you.

375
00:27:26,395 --> 00:27:28,729
I think you both know

376
00:27:28,730 --> 00:27:32,776
Chiang Shu-min is working
with Chou Lu-yung.

377
00:27:33,652 --> 00:27:35,654
[suspenseful music playing]

378
00:27:36,822 --> 00:27:39,408
I know some unknown people

379
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:43,120
are trying to lean
toward the other faction.

380
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:46,790
So, I'm wondering

381
00:27:47,958 --> 00:27:49,126
if Chou Lu-yung...

382
00:27:52,296 --> 00:27:54,256
has a list in hand.

383
00:28:00,053 --> 00:28:01,847
I want to know who they are.

384
00:28:04,474 --> 00:28:06,225
[Yi-hsuan] Let me handle it.

385
00:28:06,226 --> 00:28:08,812
[music continues]

386
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:14,109
[grunts]

387
00:28:22,868 --> 00:28:24,870
[siren wailing in distance]

388
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:34,379
Long time no see.

389
00:28:36,757 --> 00:28:37,883
How are you?

390
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:41,052
[dramatic music playing]

391
00:28:41,053 --> 00:28:42,428
Mm-hmm.

392
00:28:42,429 --> 00:28:46,266
With those dark circles,
not enough sleep?

393
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:50,729
- I'm fine.
- [Yi-hsuan] Really?

394
00:28:56,068 --> 00:28:58,320
Hearing that,
I don't have to worry.

395
00:29:08,872 --> 00:29:10,165
I've been thinking.

396
00:29:12,501 --> 00:29:15,462
Can I answer
your question properly again?

397
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:21,885
I think I've been
too focused on my goals

398
00:29:22,886 --> 00:29:24,888
that I forgot there's someone

399
00:29:26,974 --> 00:29:28,141
very important

400
00:29:29,268 --> 00:29:30,769
in my life.

401
00:29:36,024 --> 00:29:37,234
I'd like to tell you...

402
00:29:39,278 --> 00:29:41,029
- I want...
- Chou Lu-yung,

403
00:29:42,364 --> 00:29:44,408
don't fall in love
with someone who hates you.

404
00:29:47,577 --> 00:29:50,162
I'll win the battle
for Chang Da-chin.

405
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:52,081
I used to work at Jin Lai Hao.

406
00:29:52,082 --> 00:29:54,584
I know well the strengths
and weaknesses of every one
of you.

407
00:29:55,919 --> 00:29:57,963
You have only one choice.

408
00:29:58,088 --> 00:30:00,090
[tense music playing]

409
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:03,259
Give me the list
of your faction's shareholders.

410
00:30:03,260 --> 00:30:05,303
Otherwise,
I'll begin to attack Jin Lai Hao

411
00:30:05,304 --> 00:30:07,264
with the resources
from Chang Xin.

412
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:19,192
Why would I give it to you?

413
00:30:21,486 --> 00:30:24,364
Because that's the only way
you'll get close to me.

414
00:30:29,036 --> 00:30:29,995
CHAO YI-HSUAN

415
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:32,163
[Lu-yung] <i>Here's the list.</i>

416
00:30:32,164 --> 00:30:34,123
<i>Will you come back now?</i>

417
00:30:34,124 --> 00:30:37,794
[Yi-hsuan]
<i>Thanks for the list.
I'll think about it.</i>

418
00:30:37,919 --> 00:30:39,295
<i>But here's my advice.</i>

419
00:30:39,296 --> 00:30:41,590
<i>Stop fighting
against Chang Xin.</i>

420
00:30:44,051 --> 00:30:45,551
[phone buzzes]

421
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:48,180
[Secretary Chin] Sir,
the names from Chou Lu-yung

422
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:52,142
are exactly the same
as your predictions.

423
00:30:53,477 --> 00:30:55,228
[chuckles]

424
00:30:58,982 --> 00:31:02,444
Never thought that Chao Yi-hsuan
would really do it.

425
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:10,202
I thought you trusted her
in the first place.

426
00:31:11,244 --> 00:31:12,371
Trust?

427
00:31:15,165 --> 00:31:18,250
Anyone with foresight knows

428
00:31:18,251 --> 00:31:22,213
that you can't trust
what you see,

429
00:31:22,214 --> 00:31:26,510
just like how I predicted
these traitors.

430
00:31:29,054 --> 00:31:30,971
All taken care of.

431
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:33,225
But our daughter
is on her way from the States
to meet us there.

432
00:31:40,482 --> 00:31:42,692
What's wrong? What is it?

433
00:31:42,943 --> 00:31:45,237
DO NOT ATTEND THE MEETING,
OR THESE PHOTOS WON'T JUST BE
ON YOUR PHONE.

434
00:31:45,362 --> 00:31:47,864
[director]
Do you want to keep playing?

435
00:31:47,989 --> 00:31:50,450
[director's son]
Yeah. I'll have matches
next semester.

436
00:31:54,955 --> 00:31:56,164
<i>You bastard!</i>

437
00:32:04,214 --> 00:32:06,383
<i>Your pants. Where are they?</i>

438
00:32:06,508 --> 00:32:08,259
YOUR KID IS A BULLY AT SCHOOL.
HE'S TURNED 18, RIGHT?

439
00:32:08,260 --> 00:32:09,928
<i>The pants are gone.</i>

440
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:18,227
I gave them the list.

441
00:32:18,228 --> 00:32:19,729
I'm so sorry.

442
00:32:24,693 --> 00:32:27,320
Chairman Chang must have
something to hold over them.

443
00:32:33,535 --> 00:32:37,121
But perhaps, exposing
these hidden problems earlier

444
00:32:37,122 --> 00:32:38,707
may not be a bad thing
after all.

445
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:41,417
[knocks on door]

446
00:32:41,418 --> 00:32:43,086
[secretary] Catherine,
your guest is here.

447
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:48,008
[acoustic music playing]

448
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:56,600
Thanks for joining us.

449
00:32:56,725 --> 00:32:58,268
I wonder how Miss Chiang
convinced you.

450
00:33:00,061 --> 00:33:03,148
We've talked many times,
and I've thought about it
for a long time.

451
00:33:04,649 --> 00:33:06,276
But I've thought it through.

452
00:33:07,777 --> 00:33:11,198
If it goes on like this,
I might become someone like him.

453
00:33:12,574 --> 00:33:14,533
But...

454
00:33:14,534 --> 00:33:15,702
that's not what I want.

455
00:33:18,163 --> 00:33:19,664
You're welcome to join us.

456
00:33:19,789 --> 00:33:22,125
I know you won't regret
your choice.

457
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:28,631
I visited
some major shareholders.

458
00:33:28,632 --> 00:33:30,759
But I think
they've made up their minds.

459
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:33,762
I guess my dad
has already talked to them.

460
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:36,389
I'll talk
to the minority shareholders.
Do you have a list?

461
00:33:38,266 --> 00:33:43,313
These are the names
I found online, but their shares
are really small.

462
00:33:45,398 --> 00:33:48,777
It's alright. We'll spend
three or four times the time...

463
00:33:49,027 --> 00:33:51,488
- Doing it the hard way
like this won't work.
- This is our only chance.

464
00:33:51,613 --> 00:33:53,739
But it might not meet
our expectations.

465
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:56,576
If we strike,
it needs to be powerful.

466
00:33:57,577 --> 00:34:01,164
Miss Chiang, you always said
I'm the key, right?

467
00:34:19,474 --> 00:34:20,559
Hi, Dad.

468
00:34:22,811 --> 00:34:24,813
[chuckles] Well...

469
00:34:25,647 --> 00:34:28,525
Before you go abroad,
you've come to visit me.

470
00:34:29,192 --> 00:34:30,569
[Chang Ta-chin grunts]

471
00:34:31,695 --> 00:34:33,822
But I don't think
it's good for you.

472
00:34:34,698 --> 00:34:36,240
It's said that

473
00:34:36,241 --> 00:34:40,244
having too much on your mind
makes you a coward.

474
00:34:40,245 --> 00:34:41,663
[laughs]

475
00:34:43,456 --> 00:34:45,625
Dad, I'm here to tell you
I'm not going to New York.

476
00:34:51,464 --> 00:34:52,548
[sighs]

477
00:34:52,549 --> 00:34:54,466
Fine.

478
00:34:54,467 --> 00:34:55,844
Tell me about it.

479
00:34:57,220 --> 00:34:59,681
What are your reasons to stay?

480
00:35:02,225 --> 00:35:04,185
I want to build my own path.

481
00:35:16,573 --> 00:35:19,367
This magazine
will be published tomorrow.

482
00:35:20,577 --> 00:35:23,246
I don't want you
to find out from the media.

483
00:35:24,414 --> 00:35:26,415
But Dad,

484
00:35:26,416 --> 00:35:29,127
the company needs
a new business model.

485
00:35:31,254 --> 00:35:32,922
I want to prove to you

486
00:35:33,173 --> 00:35:34,633
that this is how we take
the company further.

487
00:35:34,758 --> 00:35:36,300
CHALLENGE THE EMPEROR
OF CHANG XIN

488
00:35:36,301 --> 00:35:38,094
[chuckles]

489
00:35:38,219 --> 00:35:39,304
Great.

490
00:35:40,472 --> 00:35:42,265
[laughs]

491
00:35:43,391 --> 00:35:44,684
Good job.

492
00:35:48,271 --> 00:35:49,439
Get out!

493
00:35:51,232 --> 00:35:52,483
Out!

494
00:35:52,484 --> 00:35:55,487
[dramatic music playing]

495
00:36:07,457 --> 00:36:09,167
[beeps]

496
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:12,212
[printer whirring]

497
00:36:25,684 --> 00:36:29,479
Hi. Please pass it
to the mail room and ask them
to forward it to HR.

498
00:36:29,604 --> 00:36:32,314
- [guard] Okay, consider it done.
- [Hsiu-wen]
Have a great weekend. Thank you.

499
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:33,566
[guard] You're welcome.

500
00:37:11,438 --> 00:37:13,355
[deep exhales]

501
00:37:13,356 --> 00:37:15,942
Dad, what's wrong with you?

502
00:37:18,528 --> 00:37:19,863
I'm fine.

503
00:37:21,865 --> 00:37:23,533
How have you been in there?

504
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:26,703
What do you think?

505
00:37:31,875 --> 00:37:33,835
I know you've suffered for this.

506
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:38,256
Be patient.

507
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:41,550
And behave in there.

508
00:37:41,551 --> 00:37:44,304
I believe
you'll be paroled soon.

509
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:52,562
Chiang Shu-min is calling
a shareholders' meeting.

510
00:37:53,772 --> 00:37:55,690
I think you know that.

511
00:37:56,399 --> 00:37:58,318
I got the proxy from you.

512
00:38:01,696 --> 00:38:04,656
Our management faction
and their market faction

513
00:38:04,657 --> 00:38:06,701
are so close on votes.

514
00:38:07,869 --> 00:38:10,914
- So, I really need your vote.
- [sighs]

515
00:38:14,626 --> 00:38:15,919
Dad,

516
00:38:17,295 --> 00:38:18,922
I've been in here for a while.

517
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:23,593
But the first letter
I get from you

518
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:27,639
is a proxy you want me to sign?

519
00:38:27,764 --> 00:38:29,766
[tense music playing]

520
00:38:30,850 --> 00:38:32,811
Chien-yuan,

521
00:38:32,936 --> 00:38:34,813
whether our Chang family

522
00:38:34,938 --> 00:38:40,651
can maintain control
of Chang Xin depends
on this battle.

523
00:38:40,652 --> 00:38:42,945
We must win.

524
00:38:42,946 --> 00:38:44,988
- We?
- Mm-hmm.

525
00:38:44,989 --> 00:38:46,616
Speak for yourself.

526
00:38:49,953 --> 00:38:52,622
[sighs]
Dad, I've been wondering...

527
00:38:54,874 --> 00:38:56,709
if I'm your son

528
00:38:57,877 --> 00:38:59,128
or your tool.

529
00:39:00,713 --> 00:39:03,508
Chien-yuan,
how can you say that?

530
00:39:04,801 --> 00:39:08,471
I need to hold onto the company,
so I'm able to protect you.

531
00:39:10,557 --> 00:39:12,976
[laughs]

532
00:39:21,442 --> 00:39:23,653
There you go again.

533
00:39:24,821 --> 00:39:28,699
You need to hold
onto the company,
so you're able to protect me.

534
00:39:28,700 --> 00:39:31,995
Dad, don't you have
something else to say?

535
00:39:32,829 --> 00:39:35,747
Why don't you get it?

536
00:39:35,748 --> 00:39:39,543
If we lose the company,
you and I will have nothing.

537
00:39:39,544 --> 00:39:41,879
When you get out,
you'll have nothing.

538
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:43,714
So what?

539
00:39:43,715 --> 00:39:44,841
Are you threatening me?

540
00:39:44,966 --> 00:39:47,050
I'm not threatening you.

541
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:49,052
I'm trying
to protect you, you know.

542
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:51,931
[guard]
42931, keep it down.

543
00:39:55,518 --> 00:39:57,395
Then why am I here?

544
00:39:59,981 --> 00:40:01,648
Chien-yuan,

545
00:40:01,649 --> 00:40:03,860
I can't explain it
to you in detail.

546
00:40:04,611 --> 00:40:08,197
Anyway,
it's a key moment for us.

547
00:40:08,448 --> 00:40:10,199
If you're man enough,
sign it now.

548
00:40:15,997 --> 00:40:17,123
Dad,

549
00:40:18,791 --> 00:40:20,710
you've never praised me.

550
00:40:23,713 --> 00:40:25,048
In all these years,

551
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:27,925
you've never hugged me

552
00:40:27,926 --> 00:40:31,970
or patted me on the shoulder,
telling me,

553
00:40:31,971 --> 00:40:34,641
"Chien-yuan,
thank you for your hard work."

554
00:40:35,475 --> 00:40:36,893
Nothing at all.

555
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:43,066
I'm not worth it, am I?

556
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:53,701
I've always known

557
00:40:54,911 --> 00:40:56,704
I'm not so outstanding.

558
00:40:58,581 --> 00:41:00,792
I'm not smart like Chien-wu,

559
00:41:02,085 --> 00:41:05,129
or capable like Hsiu-wen.

560
00:41:07,173 --> 00:41:08,466
But...

561
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:12,804
just because
I'm not outstanding,

562
00:41:14,764 --> 00:41:16,474
I can't be your son?

563
00:41:17,600 --> 00:41:18,685
Is that it?

564
00:41:22,981 --> 00:41:24,107
Chien-yuan,

565
00:41:27,068 --> 00:41:28,653
you are my son.

566
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:34,826
Even if you're dumb,
you're my son all the same.

567
00:41:35,994 --> 00:41:38,496
To me,
you're the most outstanding.

568
00:41:40,123 --> 00:41:43,251
And now is the best time
to prove yourself, isn't it?

569
00:41:48,798 --> 00:41:50,633
Yeah, yeah.

570
00:41:52,218 --> 00:41:54,220
You're telling me these things

571
00:41:55,513 --> 00:41:57,181
only because you need me now.

572
00:42:01,728 --> 00:42:02,979
[sighs]

573
00:42:06,858 --> 00:42:10,153
What Chao Yi-hsuan
told me is right.

574
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:14,282
She saw right through you
in an instant.

575
00:42:18,119 --> 00:42:20,163
But I've spent a lifetime

576
00:42:21,914 --> 00:42:23,833
and still
don't understand anything.

577
00:42:27,170 --> 00:42:28,920
Chao Yi-hsuan?

578
00:42:28,921 --> 00:42:31,007
[dramatic music playing]

579
00:42:35,803 --> 00:42:38,056
[singer] <i>♪ Nobody knows... ♪</i>

580
00:42:40,266 --> 00:42:42,351
- She visited me.
- [beeping]

581
00:42:42,602 --> 00:42:44,020
Chien-yuan.

582
00:42:44,979 --> 00:42:47,356
[news anchor] <i>An internal
power struggle broke out
at Chang Xin Group,</i>

583
00:42:47,607 --> 00:42:49,692
<i>the long-established
Taiwanese cuisine brand.</i>

584
00:42:49,817 --> 00:42:52,861
<i>After the original successor,
Chang Chien-yuan,
got put in jail,</i>

585
00:42:52,862 --> 00:42:55,739
<i>the younger son,
Chang Chien-wu, in a recent
magazine interview,</i>

586
00:42:55,740 --> 00:42:57,366
<i>declared for the first time</i>

587
00:42:57,617 --> 00:42:59,785
<i>that he'll challenge his father
for the chairmanship.</i>

588
00:42:59,786 --> 00:43:01,286
The vote is close,

589
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:02,871
but with our secured votes
are still slightly behind.

590
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:04,791
<i>Can we win
by vote allocation?</i>

591
00:43:07,126 --> 00:43:10,754
[singer] <i>♪ Nobody knows... ♪</i>

592
00:43:10,755 --> 00:43:12,715
[Chien-wu]
<i>Not easy. But that's all
we can do for now.</i>

593
00:43:12,840 --> 00:43:13,883
This is our only chance.

594
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:19,263
[phone beeping]

595
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:24,142
[Lu-yung] <i>No matter what,
we need to try.</i>

596
00:43:24,143 --> 00:43:27,688
[singer]
<i>♪ Fighting right here... ♪</i>

597
00:43:29,065 --> 00:43:30,983
[news anchor]
<i>Many people think this battle
between father and son</i>

598
00:43:31,234 --> 00:43:34,362
<i>may bring uncertainty
to the operations
of their restaurants.</i>

599
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:37,781
<i>With divided opinion
between company management
and shareholders,</i>

600
00:43:37,782 --> 00:43:40,785
<i>the upcoming shareholders'
meeting is going to be
the key battlefield.</i>

601
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:46,749
[credits music playing]

602
00:43:52,964 --> 00:43:56,008
[singer singing in Mandarin]
